Z||000000||Mattyman||12-29-2001||04:36 PM||||Well today I finally went out and bought a thermostat because my heat wasn't working that well.  I went to take out the old one and it wasn't there.  I'm guessing that was the problem.  Would someone of taken it out in the summer because it would overheat or what?   I put the new one in but haven't driven to see if the heat works and if the engine temp is ok.<P>------------------<BR>You gotta stand for Something or your gonna fall for everything.||||reg||1
Z||000001||shelfran||12-29-2001||04:45 PM||||Probably took it out for the summer. Make sure your fan works once you put the t stat back in...make sure your temp gauge works also. There is usually enough heat without it.<BR>Good luck,<BR>Frank Sheldon<BR>Ticonderoga, NY||||reg||1
